# Typed returns for base stubs. The base-stub generator (scripts/bc2cpp/base_rbs.rb, base_rbs_native.rb) writes these
# methods untyped, so these declarations are the only source of their types. Each class carries the marker of the base
# table it came from, as the base section's declarations do: a native declaration with no program hint, so a method the
# closed program does not define is accepted (TC1005) rather than refused (TC1003).
# bc2cpp-native: base_rgss
